If a patient has a renal-dysfunction and a clinician prescribes an ER-LA-opioid to the patient then the clinician should heed an additional-ER-LA-caution and should consider a longer-dosing-interval.
If a patient has a hepatic-dysfunction and a clinician prescribes an ER-LA-opioid to the patient then the clinician should heed an additional-ER-LA-caution and should consider a longer-dosing-interval.
A decreased-medication-clearance can cause a toxic-drug-accumulation and can cause a prolonged-drug-persistence.
